## OAuth invalid_grant retry and line-mode slash completion — 2026-11-11

User-reported regression after the browser login attempt:
- First dynamic registration reached code exchange but returned `invalid_grant`.
- The token response error did not include a useful description or request identifier.
- Scrollback-mode TUI rendered every slash-command prefix on a separate terminal line; Enter also accepted the highlighted completion rather than submitting the typed command.

Current OpenAI documentation checked 2026-11-11:
- The SIWC registration guide says to discard an `invalid_grant` authorization code and start a fresh authorization using the issued client ID.
- The error-recovery guide says `prompt=consent` remains supported for an explicit plan-access re-consent before `force_reconsent=true` is deployed. Do not force consent on ordinary sign-in.
- Sources: https://developers.openai.com/siwc/token-sharing-open-source/sign-in and https://developers.openai.com/siwc/token-sharing-open-source/errors-and-recovery

Corrections:
- OAuth now retries one `invalid_grant` with fresh state, nonce, and PKCE values and the issued registration ID; it never retries with `dynamic_agent_client`.
- The initial dynamic-registration request omits `prompt=consent`; explicit ChatGPT-plan re-consent with an issued client ID includes it.
- Token endpoint errors now retain HTTP status, OAuth error, any available description, and OpenAI request ID.
- TUI suggestion row accounting now includes the header and trailing cursor row emitted by the renderer, so prior prompt lines are erased correctly.
- In scrollback mode, Enter submits the exact typed command; Tab remains the explicit completion key.
- Added regression tests for authorization retry classification, consent behavior, prompt-row accounting, and line-mode Enter behavior.

Verification: pending GitHub Actions. No local production build. `main` remains unchanged.

